      "id": "acc73bdfb939-q6",
      "number": 6,
      "question": "Statement: According to latest census report the gender ratio has fallen further in India. Course of Action: I. The government should conduct another census to verify the results. II. The government should immediately start an awareness campaign through its public relations department about the effect of low gender ratio and encourage them to improve it.",
      "questionHtml": "<p>Statement: According to latest census report the gender ratio has fallen further in India.</p><p>Course of Action:</p><p>I. The government should conduct another census to verify the results.</p><p>II. The government should immediately start an awareness campaign through its public relations department about the effect of low gender ratio and encourage them to improve it.</p>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p>I. Conducting another census to verify the results is a valid course of action when there are doubts about the accuracy of the data. However, it may not be an immediate solution and can be resource-intensive.</p><p>II. Launching an awareness campaign to educate the public about the consequences of a low gender ratio and encourage them to improve it is a proactive approach to addressing the issue. This can be done relatively quickly and may have a positive impact on societal attitudes and behaviors.</p><p>Given this, you could argue that Course of Action II is a more appropriate immediate response to the problem mentioned in the statement. So, a more precise answer could be: (b) Only course of action II</p><p>Hence, b is the correct answer.</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
