          "html": ""
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p>Argument I: \"Yes, excess and inefficient staff is one of the reasons for the sickness of public sector organizations, though they are experienced.\" This argument suggests that one of the reasons for the sickness of public sector organizations is excess and inefficient staff, even though they are experienced. It implies that introducing schemes of voluntary retirement could help address this issue. This argument is reasonable and directly addresses the statement's concern about the sickness of public sector units. Therefore, Argument I is strong.</p><p>Argument II: \"Yes, this is what private and multinational companies do in the developed countries.\" This argument draws a parallel between public sector units and private/multinational companies in developed countries. It suggests that if private and multinational companies in developed countries implement voluntary retirement schemes, public sector units in India should do the same. While it provides a comparative perspective, it doesn't directly address the reasons behind the sickness of public sector units in India. It lacks a direct connection to the statement's concern. Therefore, Argument II is relatively weak.</p><p>So, the answer is (b) Only argument I is strong.</p>",
