      "id": "acc73bdfb939-q25",
      "number": 25,
      "question": "Statements: The railway authority has announced that it will carry out major repair work for two days beginning Saturday on the main line connecting the two big cities in the state bringing the rail service to a halt. Assumptions: I. People may reschedule their journey in view of the railway authority’s decision. II. People may still plan their travel by train between the two cities even on these two days. Identify which of the given assumption(s) are implicit in the statement.",
      "questionHtml": "<p>Statements:</p><p>The railway authority has announced that it will carry out major repair work for two days beginning Saturday on the main line connecting the two big cities in the state bringing the rail service to a halt.</p><p>Assumptions:</p><p>I. People may reschedule their journey in view of the railway authority’s decision.</p><p>II. People may still plan their travel by train between the two cities even on these two days.</p><p>Identify which of the given assumption(s) are implicit in the statement.</p>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p>I. People may reschedule their journey in view of the railway authority’s decision. This assumption suggests that people might choose to reschedule their travel plans due to the railway authority's decision to halt rail services for two days. It's a reasonable assumption, as major repair work causing a complete halt in rail services would inconvenience travelers, and many might indeed consider rescheduling their journeys to avoid this inconvenience. Therefore, Assumption I is implicit in the statement.</p><p>II. People may still plan their travel by train between the two cities even on these two days. This assumption implies that despite the announced major repair work and the halt in rail services, people may still plan to travel by train between the two cities during these two days. This assumption is not reasonable because the statement clearly states that the rail service will be brought to a halt during the repair work. Therefore, Assumption II is not implicit in the statement.</p><p>So, the answer is, [a] Only I is implicit</p><p>Assumption I is implicit in the statement as it is a reasonable inference that people may reschedule their journeys due to the announced repair work. Assumption II is not implicit because it contradicts the information provided in the statement about the halt in rail services.</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
